{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310768,"nonce":"vSQNLFjim1qF8daAxUGn29gzHz4=","title":"Haxe metadata is an expression form and the RD parser was silently discarding it; wiring it to ExprKind::Meta unblocks body-level ...","message":"**CORRECTION to an earlier belief: body-level annotations ARE standard Haxe.**\n`haxe.macro.Expr` has `EMeta(s:MetadataEntry, e:Expr)` — metadata attaches to\nEXPRESSIONS, not only declarations. `@:privateAccess sock.__s`,\n`@:bypassAccessor`, `@:nullSafety(Off)` on a block, `@:inline f()` are all legal\ninside a function body. The thing that is not allowed is a bare `inline`\n*keyword* on a statement; do not generalise from that to \"no annotations in\nbodies\". I got this wrong once and it shaped a design discussion.\n\n**What was actually broken (rayzor, not Haxe).** `parser/src/rd/expr.rs`\n`parse_unary` consumed expression metadata and threw it away:\n`let _ = self.parse_metadata_list();`. Its comment claimed \"no slot for it on\nExpr\" — **that comment was wrong**. `ExprKind::Meta { meta, expr }` exists at\n`haxe_ast.rs:762`, the legacy parser builds it, and the whole pipeline already\ncarried it: `ast_lowering.rs:9653` -\u003e `TypedExpressionKind::Meta`, handled in\n`type_checking_pipeline.rs:1786`, `effect_analysis.rs:514`,\n`dfg_builder.rs:1195`, and unwrapped transparently at\n`tast_to_hir.rs:3174`. Only the live parser dropped it.\n\nSo metadata survives through TAST — which is exactly where `@:move`,\n`@:borrow`, `@:await` would be read — and disappears at HIR.\n\n**Consequence while it was dropped:** ANY `@:whatever` on an expression was\naccepted and meant nothing. `@:totallyNotAThing b.get()` compiles fine. And\n`@:privateAccess` appeared to \"work\" only by coincidence — **rayzor does not\nenforce `private` on field access at all**; `b.secret` from outside the class\ncompiles and runs.\n\n**Probe:** `RAYZOR_META_LOG=1` prints each metadata as it lowers, with name,\nannotated expression kind and source location.\n\n**TRAP that cost time proving this:** a fresh `RAYZOR_CACHE_DIR` is NOT enough\nto force a recompile — the probe printed 0 lines until `--no-cache` was added,\nat which point the same file showed 12. Always `--no-cache` when proving a\nfront-end path executed.\n\n**Stacking nests outermost-first:** `@:a @:b e` -\u003e `Meta{a, Meta{b, e}}`, so the\ninnermost metadata sits closest to the expression it annotates.\n\nOracle: `compiler/tests/haxe/test_expr_metadata.hx` (field, call, literal,\nstacked, parameterised, as call argument, in arithmetic, in a typed binding,\nin a condition).\n\n**Open design question:** unknown expression metadata is silently accepted,\nwhich sits badly against [[feedback_no_silent_dispatch_fallthrough]]. Deciding\nwhat is a known name — and erroring otherwise — is unresolved.\n\nRelated: [[project_moveflow_mir_move_checker]] (the ownership annotations this\nreopens), [[bugs_rd_parser_issues]].\n\n- Index summary moved from MEMORY.md (2026-10-18): Body-level `@:meta expr` IS standard Haxe (EMeta); the RD parser DISCARDED it though the whole pipeline carried it. Now builds ExprKind::Meta. `RAYZOR_META_LOG=1`. TRAP: needs `--no-cache` to prove. `private` is NOT enforced.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `feature_expression_metadata_rd_parser` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}